## Test files written this session

- `test/app-route.test.ts` — UPDATED (additive extension, matching the file's own established "ADDITIVE" convention from a prior phase): added `taskRouteOf`/`taskIdFromRoute` imports and four new `describe` blocks covering the Task route (`/tasks/:id` <-> `task/${id}`), the bare-`/tasks` and nested-path edge cases, and the AC-8 headline round-trip (`pathOf(routeFromPath(p)) === p`) for a Task path. Every pre-existing assertion (today/settings/notifications/notifications-diagnostics round-trips, the unrecognised-path default) is untouched — this is also where AC-A5's "existing routes still round-trip unchanged" requirement is independently satisfied by the pre-existing, unmodified test cases.
- `test/task-sheet.test.ts` — UPDATED (additive extension, no existing test modified): added two new `describe` blocks covering `open-reminder`/`close-reminder` and `request-delete-reminder`/`cancel-delete-reminder`, including the no-op-when-`taskId`-null guard on each of the four new events and, as the headline assertion, that `cancel-delete-reminder` lands on `"reminder"` and NOT on `"detail"` — the exact discrimination the plan names as the defect three prior revisions exist to close. A final check confirms the pre-existing Task-delete pair (`request-delete`/`cancel-delete`) is untouched by the new reminder pair.
- `test/dates.test.ts` — UPDATED (additive extension, no existing test modified): added coverage for the newly-exported `offsetMinutesAt` (fixed -180 min for America/Sao_Paulo, 0 for UTC) and the two new functions `instantToLocalParts`/`localPartsToInstant` — conversion both ways, timezone defaulting and overriding, a local-day-boundary crossing case, a clock-independence check (mirroring the existing `offsetToInstant` fixture style), and a round-trip check between the two new functions.
- `test/reminder-edit.test.ts` — CREATE: `draftFromReminder` (create-seed default, restoring each of the three live Reminder shapes — Task-linked offset, standalone absolute, Task-linked absolute — and the null-label-to-empty-string mapping), `buildCreateReminderInput` (standalone absolute path, label trim-to-null, the "offset with no Task target falls back to fireAt" guard, and the Task-linked offset-vs-absolute branch), and `buildUpdateReminderInput` (empty patch on no change, single-field diffs, and the two mode-transition special cases — offset-to-absolute clears `originOffsetMinutes`, absolute-to-offset emits the new `originOffsetMinutes`).
- `test/cron-reminder-route.test.ts` — CREATE: two tests against `runScheduledJob`, mocking only `sendPush` (the documented thin/exempt network adapter) to capture the plaintext payload argument before encryption — a Task-linked Reminder's dispatched payload carries `pathOf(taskRouteOf(taskId))` and round-trips through `routeFromPath`/`pathOf`; a standalone Reminder's payload still carries `"/"`.

